NOTE ON THE SCHEMA FILES

spec/bio.xsd, spec/bio.libxml.xsd and spec/bio.sch are additionally released into the
public domain under CC0 1.0.

This is deliberate. A schema gets embedded in tools, generated code, and other people's
formats, and an attribution requirement on it is friction that serves nobody. Take them,
change them, ship them, fork the vocabulary, build something incompatible. No attribution
required and no permission needed.

Attribution is still appreciated, and if you extend the vocabulary usefully we would rather
hear about it than not.

NOTE ON THE DOCUMENTATION

The specification prose and dossiers in spec/ and dossier/ are additionally offered
under CC BY 4.0, so they can be quoted and adapted in academic work with attribution.

The 3MF Consortium's own specifications, from which this schema borrows structure and
conventions, carry their own licence and disclaimer; see 3mf.io. This project is not
affiliated with them.

The dossiers cite third-party standards and publications. Citation is not
redistribution: ISO, ASTM and other standards remain the copyright of their
publishers and must be obtained from them.
